From 169c3f240047fbe579fdc8627411fe9a07d2c4b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Coinupbtc <coinupbtc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:33:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dsv41: read a finished reply ahead while the client runs its
 tools, and keep the state there (TF_DS_STEP_AHEAD)

An agent's next request is its last prompt, the reply, and the tool results. The prompt cache keeps states only at
chunk ends of a prompt pass, so that request resumed at its previous prompt's last kept chunk end and read the whole
reply again before the new tokens: on one owner's agent traffic (248 chained requests at 30-175K tokens) two thirds
of every step's prompt pass was its own previous reply.

With TF_DS_STEP_AHEAD=1 (default unset: off, the engine unchanged), when a reply ends and nothing else runs or
waits, rank 0 queues a background prompt pass of prompt ++ reply, cut at the last chunk end of the family's grid that
leaves the window (dsv41: 2,048-row chunks, 128 tokens), with its history mark there. The pass resumes the
conversation's latest kept state and keeps one at that chunk end. It is the next request's own cold pass up to
there (the same grid, the same tokens), so a request that resumes it gets the bytes a cold pass gets; its tokens
must equal the reply as the template renders it back, else it resumes where it did before. A queued pass yields to
any arrival, a running one is cancelled by an arrival that does not continue it, and it never runs beside another
stream. One token, no drafts.

Tests: lane_host_reuse_test.zig: the pass keeps the grid point and the next step resumes there with the fake's
history-checked tokens; nothing runs when off or when a reply moves no kept state a chunk on.
